  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member using the dense rows (Réglages › Expérimental, #905), I want the « MP multiples » rows as compact as the dense topic rows, so that both lists read the same way, on one info line.\n\n### Wanted (operator, 2026-11-16), dense view, « MP multiples » rows\n\n- **A.** No « Interlocuteurs multiples » mention.\n- **B.** No reply count.\n- **C.** The pages as **« ⚑ flag page / total pages »** (the page of the member's flag in the thread, then the thread's page count).\n- **D.** No « il y a » in the relative date (« 6 min », « 2 h », then the date).\n- **E.** The info line **never wraps**: if it does not fit on one line, it ends with « … ».\n\n### Consistency with the dense topic rows (#905, operator decision of 2026-11-16)\n\n| Rule | Topics, dense (#905) | MP multiples, dense (this issue) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Who | the last poster instead of the topic starter (C) | the last poster (already shown); no « Interlocuteurs multiples » (A) |\n| Count | no reply count (D) | no reply count (B) ✓ |\n| Pages | « ⚑ lue / total » | « ⚑ flag page / total pages » (C) ✓ same format |\n| Date | no « il y a » (E) | no « il y a » (D) ✓ |\n| Line | one line, « … » when it does not fit (E) | the same (E) ✓ |\n| Section titles in bold (F) | yes | not applicable (no sections in the MP list) |\n\nOne formatter for both dense rows (topic and MP), so the rules cannot drift apart. The one-to-one « MP » rows in dense view follow the same B, D and E (their interlocutor replaces A).\n\n### Scope\n\n- The dense row code behind `EXPERIMENTAL(denseRows, #905)`. The default rows (#817, #900) are unchanged.\n- **Grouped with #905:** the same child, the same PR.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Tests on the shared dense formatter: no « Interlocuteurs multiples », no reply count, « ⚑ x / y », no « il y a », and a single line with truncation.\n- [ ] Device check in the general review.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
